       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in PMR:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " sarilumab (IL-6 inhibitor) for inadeq response to corticosteroids or inability to tolerate dose ↓; TNF inhibitors (infliximab, adalimumab) haven't shown benefit"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) dose, polymyalgia rheumatica (PMR):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " PMR: 200 mg SC once every two wks in combo w tapering course of systemic corticosteroids - may be used as monotx following d/c of corticosteroids"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ↑risk of serious infect that may lead to hsp or death; opportunistic infect also reported; ⍉use in pts w active infect. Prior to starting KEVZARA, test for latent TB - if (+), start tx for TB"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " known hypersensitivity to sarilumab or any inactive ingredients"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) neutropenia/CBC screening:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ⍉initiate KEVZARA in pts w ANC < 2,000/mm3, PLT < 150,000/mm3, or liver transaminases above 1.5 × ULN. Assess ANC prior to initiation & monitor 4 to 8 wks after start of therapy & every 3 mo thereafter. D/c KEVZARA in PMR pts who develop neutropenia (ANC below 1,000 per mm3 @ end of the dosing interval) · thrombocytopenia (PLT below 100,000 per mm3) or AST or ALT elevations 3 × above the ULN"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) LFT monitoring:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Assess ALT & AST prior to initiation & monitor 4 to 8 wks after start of therapy & every 3 mo thereafter - when clinically indicated, consider other LFTs such as bili"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) GI perf:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " GI perforations reported, primarily as comp of diverticulitis; risk may be ↑ w concurrent diverticulitis or concomitant NSAIDs or corticosteroids - promptly evaluate pts presenting w new onset abd Sx"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
